**Your role, your impact**
 As an Azure DevOps Engineer, you’ll support and enhance CI/CD pipelines and infrastructure deployments in Microsoft Azure. Working in an enterprise environment, you’ll focus on security and change management, collaborating closely with senior engineers. Your strong engineering foundation and hands\-on automation and infrastructure\-as\-code experience will be essential to your success. You’ll also have opportunities to deepen your technical expertise.








**Your day\-to\-day**
* Build, maintain, and troubleshoot CI/CD pipelines using Azure DevOps;
* Develop and modify ARM templates and Bicep code for Azure environments;
* Automate deployments across development, QA, and production using PowerShell and scripting;
* Deploy and support Azure infrastructure, including VMs, networking, and PaaS resources;
* Assist with security hardening and remediation activities;
* Work with configuration and release tools (GitHub, VSTS, Artifactory, GitLab, Maven);
* Follow enterprise change management practices;
* Apply best practices for software build and release management under guidance.






**Keys to your success**
* Degree in computer science, engineering, or equivalent experience;
* 1 to 5 years of experience in DevOps or cloud engineering roles;
* Hands\-on experience with CI/CD pipelines and Azure DevOps;
* Experience deploying Azure services using infrastructure\-as\-code;
* Working knowledge of ARM, Bicep, GitHub, and PowerShell automation;
* Ability to contribute to Azure infrastructure designs and follow change management frameworks;
* Strong problem\-solving skills and ability to work with moderate supervision.


**Extra edge**
* ServiceNow CHG exposure.


**Language Skills**
 English: Proficient








